data: {"type": "thought", "agent_id": "repair-2", "text": "Rationale: BD_pump_r was mistakenly placed at (390, 165) on the PBS1->M1 segment because the counter-propagating pump actually reflects UP (+90 deg) at BS and then RIGHT (0 deg) at M1 before being transmitted through PBS1, and the BS->M1 spacing was only 35 mm causing mount/beam collisions; I increased the BS distance from M1 to 40 mm (with M4 at 80 mm to keep y=45) and placed a single dump BD_pum"}

